       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/ft113cg5195.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "stamped, not written, running along the roll; read from crop 2 turned a quarter turn. Every figure is plain, 1 6 4 2 8, the 4 with its apex and crossbar and the 8 with both counters open, and five figures admit only the parse 16.4.28. The confidence is medium not for the figures but for the parse: a stamp of five figures could in principle be a serial rather than a date, though 16428 is too long for a Welte catalogue number, and 1928 falls after the 1904 to 1926 range of the dates read so far in this corpus. A broken partial impression stands just before the 1 and is not legible. Crop 1 shows a tear repair patch and perforations, no writing."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
